  "id": "least-squares-regression",
  "term": "least squares regression",
  "definition": "Least squares regression is a method that learns a mapping from input data to target labels by minimizing the average squared difference between predicted outputs and the labels. In classification, it projects cases into a label space, but standard forms may separate different classes poorly and may not preserve similarity within the same class.",
